  "body": "Found in the review fix of PR #2659 (issue #2597, blocker B1).\n\nWhat happens:\n- In a whole-model 2D Contour, a ring whose outline grows below Top Z must step down from the stock top (#2597).\n- When the stock top is one stepdown or more over Top Z, only a pass at Top Z keeps the first bite of that ring as small as the bite of band 0. So the ring takes Top Z (`upper_levels` in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_whole_reach.rs`).\n- Band 0 also cuts its ring at Top Z. When the grown ring is closer to that ring than the lead length, the lead of one ring crosses the other ring at the same Z.\n- The verifier reports `Crossing` and blocks the post. The result is visible and safe, but a correct part does not post.\n\nEvidence:\n- `crates/app/tests/contour_whole_step.rs` case 1 (chamfered island, Top Z 15, stepdown 3.5, linear lead 8 mm) with the stock box `dz` 18.5: `Crossing { moves: [3, 27] }`. Move 3 is the lead-in of the island-top ring at Z 15. Move 27 is a corner of the grown island ring 1 mm outside it, also at Z 15.\n- With the stock top 17 (less than one stepdown over Top Z) the grown ring takes Z 13.5 and no crossing occurs. That case is pinned.\n\nExpected: the part posts, and each first bite stays at most the larger of the stepdown and the band-0 bite. Possible ways: cut the grown ring at Top Z in the band-0 emission, or select a lead that does not cross a ring of the same level. Do not hide the `Crossing` law.\n\nDone means: case 1 of `contour_whole_step` with the stock top 18.5 posts with no blocking warning, and each ring still steps down from the stock top. A pinning test covers it.\n",
